      "id": "0cbb78476f16a5d8d8808a498951c3c5e9ef669159cb0a4a639f4ea6dc201e52",
      "title": "Cannes Lions Scholarship 2027 (Fully-funded)",
      "url": "https://opportunitydesk.org/2026/11/05/cannes-lions-scholarship-2027",
      "category": "opportunities",
      "checkedAt": "2026-11-16T06:35:08.112Z",
      "httpStatus": 200,
      "finalUrl": "https://www.canneslions.com/impact/lions-scholarship",
      "contentType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
      "pageTitle": "The LIONS Scholarship | Cannes Lions",
      "pageDescription": "For Cannes Lions 2027, we’re once again offering 10 fully funded scholarships to underrepresented talent within the creative industry.",
      "evidenceText": "The LIONS Scholarship | Cannes Lions Skip to main content The LIONS Scholarship Supporting the next generation of creative talent. Apply now for 2027 For Cannes Lions 2027, we’re offering 10 fully funded scholarships to underrepresented talent within the creative industry. What’s the LIONS Scholarship? The LIONS Scholarship is designed to support the next generation of talent, placing an emphasis on diversity of location, gender, race, class, preference and perspective. With five places available in the Brand Marketers Academy and five in the Creative Academy, a total of 10 under-30s from 10 countries will be accepted for the Scholarship. The LIONS Academies Five places available on each of the following academies. Creative Academy We encourage all creatives to apply including, but not limited to, Art Directors, Copywriters, Graphic/UX Designers, Directors, Journalists, PR, Creative Technologists and Engineers. More about the Academy Brand Marketing Academy We encourage brand/client-side marketers to apply including, but not limited to Brand and Marketing Managers, Digital Marketers, Marketing Directors and Social Media Managers. More about the Academy What’s included? If you’re selected, you’ll get a fully funded trip to Cannes Lions 2027, including accommodation, travel and allowance. You’ll also get a Young Lions Festival pass, which will give you access to inspiring classroom sessions with world-class speakers, hands-on learning and coaching from industry legends. Who can apply? Applications are open to people born on or after 25 June 1996. The minimum age for applying is 18 years old, and proof of age will be required. You’ll also need to have a minimum of two years’ work experience in a role to be eligible. The LIONS Academies are presented in English. How do you select who gets to join the programme? Every year, we receive hundreds of applications for the LIONS Scholarship – and we judge every application through a two-stage process. After your initial application, we use a jury of over 40 creatives to create a shortlist. Our jurors are creative directors, art directors, creative partners and copywriters from around the world, so they know exactly what creative excellence looks like and who has the potential to reach it. Important dates Applications open: 29 October 2026, 00:01 GMT Applications close: 4 December 2026, 00:01 GMT Applicants notified: 1 February 2027 It’s a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity to learn, grow, and experience the world of marketing and creativity on a global stage. Being selected through a global competition, with all expenses covered, makes the experience even more meaningful. You don’t have to worry about logistics—just get on the plane immerse yourself in the world of creativity. Tauhid Irteza Ali Brand Marketing Senior Manager Banglalink Digital Communications Ltd. The LIONS Scholarship Entry Kit We’ve put together an entry kit to give you extra information about the programme and guidance on what to expect from the application process. Our goal is to ensure that all applicants feel supported in sharing their mission and passion for the creative industry. Get the Entry Kit Please read our FAQs Would you like to be part of it? Apply for our 2027 cohort. Apply Contact information If you have any further questions that weren’t addressed in the FAQs or need help with your application, please contact talentprogrammes@canneslions.com . LIONS Scholarship Cohort 2026 Abraham Reinaldo Zavala Treviño Abraham Reinaldo Zavala Treviño Tecate Sr. Brand Executive Heineken México Ayoyemi Oladipo Ayoyemi Oladipo Writer and Content Producer Freelance Carolina Chaparro Carolina Chaparro Brand Manager Alicorp Catherine Nathasya Catherine Nathasya Copywriter Dentsu Creative Javaad Ahmed Javaad Ahmed Creative Talented Kaelan Ashford-Jones Kaelan Ashford-Jones Sr. Coordinator, Global Brand Marketing Major League Baseball Le Ngoc Thien Trang Le Ngoc Thien Trang Business Development Manager NESTLÉ Marion Manabat Marion Manabat Senior Art Director Ogilvy Merlyn Koh Merlyn Koh Product Marketing Manager Google Sabrina Rachid Sabrina Rachid Motion Designer GUT Design Would you like to be part of it? Apply for our 2027 cohort. Apply",
