      "pageDescription": "The International Budget Partnership (IBP) Nigeria, in partnership with the Westminster Foundation for Democracy (WFD) Nigeria, is organising a Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship Workshop to strengthen journalists&#39; understanding of public debt, government borrowing, fiscal accountability and how debt decisions affect public services and citizens.\nThe fellowship is intended for practising journalists who have experience reporting on public finance issues, including government budgets, revenue, public expenditure, procurement, fiscal transparency or accountability in the management of public resources.\nJournalists covering different sectors are welcome, provided their reporting has engaged with public finance issues. Previous experience reporting specifically on public debt is not",
