e to evaluating innovative projects. Connect globally:  Engage with professionals and changemakers from diverse backgrounds. Support young leaders:  Help identify initiatives with the potential to create lasting change. Who can apply? We welcome applications from professionals with experience in social impact, entrepreneurship, innovation, sustainability, international development, project management, monitoring and evaluation, education, gender equality and related fields. Applicants should demonstrate sound judgement, integrity and a commitment to supporting young changemakers. Previous judging or project evaluation experience is an advantage. Responsibilities Selected judges will review applications, assess project innovation, community impact and sustainability, and contribute to a fair and transparent selection process. How to apply Interested applicants should complete the online application form, providing details of their professional experience, expertise and motivation for joining the judging panel. Deadline: November 30, 2026 – Click here to apply Lend Your Expertise. Discover Changemakers. Shape Global Impact. Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Global Changemakers’ Media Impact Academy 2027 for Youth in the USA (A chance to win a $1,000 grant) Next Article Arewa Creative Writing and Advocacy Fellowship (ACWAF) 2026 – Cohort 1 Favour Abatang Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram LinkedIn Favour Abatang is a Non-profit Executive and International Development Expert with experience leading an organisation, curating programs, and fundraising. She has made significant strides in supporting teenage mothers and at-risk girls through tailored second-chance opportunities. She is currently expanding her impact as the Community Manager at Opportunity Desk. Related Posts 21 Hot Job Opportunities Currently Open – November 7, 2026 November 7, 2026 How to Turn Your Passion into Income: 5 Practical Ways to Make Money Doing What 