eo Basics for Journalists Learn how to create vertical video for journalism and social media. This beginner-friendly, on-demand course teaches journalists to script, film, edit and publish videos for TikTok, Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts and other platforms, with the opportunity to earn a certificate of completion after passing the final assessment. Start Anytime Overview Start anytime with approximately two hours of self-directed, on-demand video training. Earn a certificate of completion when you finish the course. Learn vertical video storytelling specifically for journalism and original reporting. Script, film, edit and publish short-form social video. Learn approaches for TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts. Build confidence on camera and develop your social media voice. Create a repeatable vertical video workflow using tools you already have. Track video metrics and use the data to improve your strategy. Learn how to communicate video results to editors and newsroom leaders. Download five templates and tools to use after the course. Vertical Video Basics for Journalists quantity Enroll Now SKU: 82619 Tags: Certificate , front page course , Self-directed course Learning Outcomes By the end of this course, you will: Learn how to turn original reporting into compelling vertical video. Script short-form videos using visual-first storytelling techniques. Film and edit 9:16 video for TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts. Develop an authentic social media voice and greater confidence on camera. Build a repeatable workflow for creating and publishing social video. Develop a test-and-learn strategy for vertical video experimentation. Analyze video metrics to understand what resonates with audiences. Communicate social video results and insights to newsroom leaders. Sale New Certificate $ 99.00 Original price was: $99.00. $ 75.00 Current price is: $75.00. Vertical Video Basics for Journalists quantity Enroll Now Overview Start anytime with approximately two hours of self-directed, on-demand video training. Earn a certificate of completion when you finish the course. Learn vertical video storytelling specifically for journalism and original reporting. Script, film, edit and publish short-form social video. Learn approaches for TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts. Build confidence on camera and develop your social media voice. Create a repeatable vertical video workflow using tools you already have. Track video metrics and use the data to improve your strategy. Learn how to communicate video results to editors and newsroom leaders. Download five templates and tools to use after the course. Training 5 or More People? get consulting & coaching Description Schedule Requirements Learn vertical video storytelling for journalism Vertical video is how news audiences are consuming content today. For journalists, knowing how to turn original reporting into compelling vertical video for TikTok, Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts and other social platforms has become an essential storytelling skill. Vertical Video Basics for Journalists is a beginner-friendly, self-directed vertical video course for journalists who want their work to be seen, trusted and shared. Learn at your own pace and earn a certificate of completion while building practical skills in scripting, filming and editing social media video, developing your on-camera presence and social voice, and turning your reporting into visual stories designed for the way people consume news on social platforms. Led by Poynter audience engagement experts Josie Hollingsworth, TyLisa C. Johnson and Ellen Hine, the course gives you practical video storytelling strategies, frameworks and downloadable tools you can return to whenever you’re creating your next video. You’ll also learn how to track video metrics, test your social video strategy and communicate what the data tells you to editors and newsroom leaders. The course is designed for journalists who are new to vertical video or early in their social video journey. You don’t need professional equipment or previous video production experience, just a smartphone or camera and access to an editing tool. Put what you learn into practice with five resources you can return to whenever you’re planning, creating or evaluating a video: Social media persona worksheet: Define your social voice and how you want to show up for your audience. Visual-first script template: Plan your story around what your audience will see as well as what they’ll hear. Social video story structure template: Give your vertical videos a clear, engaging narrative structure. Social video upload checklist: Make sure your video is ready before you publish. Video metrics data tracker: Track results, spot patterns and build the data story behind your video strategy. Start anytime, learn at your own pace, earn a certificate of completion and leave with a repeatable process for creating short-form video from your journalism.   Why learn with Poynter? The Poynter Institute is a global nonprofit working to strengthen journalism to help address society’s most pressing problems. The world’s top journalists and emerging media leaders rely on the Institute to learn new skills, adopt best practices, better serve audiences, scale operations and foster trustworthy information. This course is taught by Poynter’s audience engagement team, combining journalism expertise with practical experience in social media, audience development and digital storytelling. Over the past few years, Poynter has leaned into video as a key part of our audience engagement and journalism work. Today, Poynter’s social brands reach 700,000 users on video platforms each month, and we’ve launched 10 video series across three brands in five years. Poynter’s vertical video experience extends across its brands, including MediaWise and PolitiFact , with initiatives such as MediaWise’s Teen Creator Network and collaborations with creators such as Dave Jorgenson of Local News International and V Spehar of Under the Desk News. To give you a sense of what we’ve learned and the content we’ve created along the way, we’ve put together some of our video highlights.   Questions? If you need assistance, email us at info@poynter.org . Virtual, self-directed course Start anytime and learn at your own pace. When you enroll, you’ll get immediate access to approximately two hours of on-demand instruction, hands-on activities and a toolkit with five downloadable resources you can use as you create your own vertical videos. Led by Poynter audience engagement experts Josie Hollingsworth, TyLisa C. Johnson and Ellen Hine, the course will teach you how to: Turn original reporting into a compelling vertical video story. Develop your social media voice and become more comfortable on camera. Script, film and edit vertical video using a visual-first approach. Build a test-and-learn strategy for yourself or your newsroom. Track video performance and identify what’s working with your audience. Tell the story behind your data to editors and newsroom leaders, turning video metrics into insights that can inform your strategy and next steps. Because this is a self-directed, on-demand course, there’s no live session to attend and no recording to wait for. You can revisit the instructions, activities and resources whenever you need them. Complete a randomized final assessment and answer at least five questions correctly to earn your certificate of completion. Who is this vertical video course for? This course is designed for journalists who are new to vertical video or early in their social video journey. It’s a good fit if: You’ve never filmed, edited or published a vertical video before. You’ve tried TikTok, Reels or Shorts but aren’t sure what makes an effective journalism video. You want a repeatable process for turning reporting into social video. You want to become more comfortable presenting journalism on camera. You’re creating social video for a newsroom or news organization. You’re a journalist independently building an audience around your reporting. You want to understand video metrics and improve your strategy over time. What do I need to take the course? You’ll need: A smartphone or camera capable of recording 9:16 vertical video Access to Google Drive Access to a vertical video editing tool You can use TikTok, Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts, CapCut, Instagram Edits or another vertical video editor. You do not need to purchase or learn one specific editing platform to complete the course.   FAQ Is this vertical video course for beginners? Yes. The course is designed for journalists who are new to vertical video or early in their journey. You do not need previous video production experience. Do I need professional video equipment? No. You can complete the course using a smartphone or another camera capable of recording vertical 9:16 video. Which social media platforms does the course cover? The principles can be applied across short-form video platforms, including TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts. Which video editing software do I need? You can use TikTok, Instagram Reels, YouTube Shorts, CapCut, Instagram Edits or another vertical video editor. Will I learn how to make TikToks and Instagram Reels from my reporting? Yes. You’ll learn a process for turning original journalism into short-form, vertical social video, including scripting, filming, editing and publishing. Will I learn how to be on camera? Yes. The course covers developing your social media voice and becoming more comfortable presenting your journalism on camera. Does the course cover video analytics? Yes. You’ll learn how to track video performance, evaluate your experiments and communicate results to editors and newsroom leaders. How long is the course? The course includes approximately two hours of on-demand instruction plus activities and downloadable resources. When can I start? Immediately after enrolling. The course is self-directed and can be completed on your own schedule. What resources are included? You’ll receive five downloadable resources: a social media persona worksheet, visual-first script template, social video story structure template, social video upload checklist and video metrics data tracker. Instructors Josie Hollingsworth Audience Director Josie Hollingsworth is Poynter’s Audience Director. As manager of the Poynter Audience Team (Home of Poynter Memes), she is responsible for digital engagement strategy, PolitiFact... Read More Ellen Hine Senior Audience Engagement Producer, PolitiFact Ellen Hine is the senior audience engagement producer with PolitiFact with a passion for connecting people to the information that will help them lead their... Read More TyLisa Johnson Audience Engagement Producer TyLisa C. Johnson is Poynter's audience engagement producer. She is an award-winning reporter who previously wrote about social and cultural topics including hunger, libraries and pandemic... Read More \"> Related Products Sale Online , St. Petersburg, Fla. Covering Jails and Police Reform (January 2022) $ 50.00 Original price was: $50.00. $ 0.00 Current price is: $0.00. Certificate Online Getting It Right: Accuracy and Verification in the Digital Age $ 50.00 Certificate Online Clarity is Key: Making Writing Clean and Concise $ 50.00 Sale Online Journalism Fundamentals: Craft & Values $ 50.00 Original price was: $50.00. $ 10.00 Current price is: $10.00.",
